# L §5.9 Rows replaced: "On a day of its span where no table is in force, only a whole table stands, as an input's
# replace row is its value where no earlier row governs". v1's table governs 2026..2027; v2's whole replacing table
# governs 2027..: in 2027 it replaces v1's wholly, b(15) = 5 (q1); in 2028 no table is in force and it stands, b(15) =
# 5 (q2); in 2026 v1's, 2 (q3). The row is held past the cut (L §8.2 held:). (Writer 8, sixth pass, beside C3-16: snap11
# refused q2 LOAD-REPLACE at the read, which refused the whole model.)
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2027-01-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2028-12-31

source s "s"
band b(n: int): int
input mid: int

version v1
  cite s
  governs 2026..2027
  known 2025-12-01
  b: [0, 10] = 1
  b: (10, inf) = 2

version facts
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2025-12-01
  mid = 15

version v2
  cite s
  governs 2027..
  known 2026-12-01
  replace b: [0, 20] = 5
  replace b: (20, inf) = 6

ask q1: b(mid) law 2027-06-30
ask q2: b(mid) law 2028-06-30
ask q3: b(mid) law 2026-06-30
=== expect
q1: 5
  held: b row [0, 20] (v2), read for 2027-06-30
  law date 2027-06-30, cut 2027-01-01
q2: 5
  held: b row [0, 20] (v2), read for 2028-06-30
  law date 2028-06-30, cut 2027-01-01
q3: 2
  law date 2026-06-30, cut 2027-01-01
